From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeavyGee <gc@lockhouse.systems>
Date: Mon, 24 Nov 2026 14:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(soup): drop the duplicate prepareCursorImportForMachine

The tip-forward merge of origin/main lands `prepareCursorImportForMachine`
TWICE in hub/src/sync/syncEngine.ts — once from upstream's #945 squash (now on
fork main) and once from the old tip's copy of the same work. The two are
functionally identical: same parameters, same single-line delegation to
`this.rpcGateway.prepareCursorImportForMachine`, differing only in whether the
signature is wrapped. TypeScript rejects it:

  src/sync/syncEngine.ts(7983,11): error TS2393: Duplicate function implementation.
  src/sync/syncEngine.ts(8003,11): error TS2393: Duplicate function implementation.

THIS LIVES IN A HEAL RATHER THAN THE MERGE RESOLUTION, and the reason is the
whole point. syncEngine.ts does NOT conflict during the tip-forward merge — both
sides add the method in a different place, so git auto-merges both copies as
context with no marker at all. rerere only replays regions that actually
conflicted, so a fix made here by hand is silently dropped by the next
recompose. Proven the hard way on 2026-11-24: the identical fix was committed to
driver/integration-wip, the remat reset the branch, and the error came straight
back — while the same-day fixes to apiMachine.ts and rpcGateway.ts DID survive,
because those files were genuinely conflicted and rerere had resolutions to
replay.

Retire this heal once the old tip no longer carries the #945 layer's copy (the
layer itself was retired 2026-11-24, so the next full recompose from main should
make this unnecessary — verify by checking the method count before deleting).
---
diff --git a/hub/src/sync/syncEngine.ts b/hub/src/sync/syncEngine.ts
index aff737358..4bbda08ce 100644
--- a/hub/src/sync/syncEngine.ts
+++ b/hub/src/sync/syncEngine.ts
@@ -8000,14 +8000,6 @@ recordSessionActivity(sessionId: string, updatedAt: number): void {
         return await this.rpcGateway.listLocalSessionsForMachine(machineId, params)
     }
 
-    async prepareCursorImportForMachine(
-        machineId: string,
-        uuid: string,
-        workspacePath?: string | null
-    ) {
-        return await this.rpcGateway.prepareCursorImportForMachine(machineId, uuid, workspacePath)
-    }
-
     async listCursorModelsForSession(sessionId: string): Promise<RpcListCursorModelsResponse> {
         return await this.rpcGateway.listCursorModelsForSession(sessionId)
     }
-- 
